From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 15 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tmpfiles: create /var/cache/xdg, traversable by service users

webos-global.conf.in sets

    DefaultEnvironment=XDG_CACHE_HOME=/var/cache/xdg

but nothing ever creates that directory, so it is made by whichever root
service touches it first and ends up 0700 root:root.

That breaks any service which caches there and then drops privileges. Atlas
does exactly this: browser_shell runs with
--user-data-dir=/var/cache/xdg/browser_shell-0, calls setgid/setuid to wam,
and can no longer traverse the 0700 parent to reach its own profile. Chromium
then aborts opening its history database:

    [FATAL:url_database.cc(38)] Check failed: db_.Open(db_file_path_).
    URLDatabase Open Operation Failed

The per-service subdirectory is already created wam-owned by
run_browser_shell, so only the parent needs to be enterable. 0711 grants
traversal without letting anyone list the directory.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 common/etc/tmpfiles.d/31-var.conf.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/common/etc/tmpfiles.d/31-var.conf.in
+++ b/common/etc/tmpfiles.d/31-var.conf.in
@@ -19,4 +19,5 @@
 d        /var/home/root              -       -      -
 d        /var/tmp                    -       -      -
 d        /var/file-cache             -       -      -
+d        /var/cache/xdg              0711    root   root
 L        @WEBOS_INSTALL_LOCALSTATEDIR@/spool/rdxd/previous_boot_logs.tar.gz - - - - @WEBOS_INSTALL_LOGDIR@/previous_boot_logs.tar.gz
